people have been writing in saying David  you haven't been talking about the  YouTube advertiser boycott for a while  can you explain what's going on because  we're seeing ads on your YouTube videos  this is a tough thing Pat because I  don't want to just talk about the  YouTube advertiser boycott because in  the same way that with the Trump  administration when everything is a  scandal nothing is a scandal if the  YouTube ad boycott is a crisis every  single day it becomes background noise  and it also becomes fatiguing for the  audience so it's been a while now since  we've talked about the YouTube  advertiser boycott but I'll give you a  quick update okay if you don't know what  I'm talking about on March 31st YouTube  put in place a new algorithm to  determine when advertisements play  before YouTube videos that's how we make  money on YouTube when ads play before a  video of ours okay and on March 31st  when this new ad algorithm was turned on  in response to concerns from advertisers  about the algorithm not being strict  enough our YouTube revenue went down 99  plus percent it doesn't even matter  exactly what it is it went down to  effectively nothing okay and it lasted  nearly two weeks at nothing April 11 and  12 we saw a little spike very small  spike in YouTube revenue maybe about 10  percent back to our 10% of our old  revenue but then on April 13th through  April 22nd it fell off a cliff again and  we were essentially making nothing okay  so what's been going on since April 22nd  which is basically the last time we  talked about this the data I had at the  time went through April 22nd I believe  roughly plus or minus one day okay two  different measures to talk about number  one before the YouTube ad boycott we had  a 60 percent monetization rate that  meant that on average for every 10 video  views on our channel 6 ads played ok now  you as an individual might say you know  I was only getting like one ad every 10  videos or I was getting an ad on like  every video that's fine at the channel  level we were getting about 6 ads for  every 10 videos during the crisis we  were at 6 to 7% monetization which me  that we had fewer than one AD per ten  videos playing now we are at about 40%  monetization okay which is about 50 I'm  sorry  one-third less it's about two-thirds of  where we were before we used to get six  ads every ten videos now we're at four  now that might sound Pat like it's great  like we're making two-thirds of what we  were making before but it is not just  how many ads play that matters it is the  quality of the ads and this is really  where we're getting crushed before the  YouTube ad boycott there's a bunch of  different types of YouTube ads some are  called auction ads some are called  reserve ads reserve ads are the good  quality ads that pay way more auction  ads are sort of the bottom of the barrel  as the name suggests it's sort of what's  left over for advertisers to bid on when  there are not enough reserve ads to play  prior to the boycott half of our ads  were reserve ads good quality ads that  pay anywhere from 50 to 100 percent more  than auction quality ads we used to have  50 percent reserve ads we now have two  percent reserve ads two percent reserve  ads so basically we've got two thirds of  the ads that we used to have and the ads  are paying about half of what they were  so simple math multiplication of  fractions tells us two thirds times one  half equals one-third so we're basically  that what I'm getting at is we have  about a third of the YouTube revenue  back from what we had before it's not  losing 99 percent but this is still a  problem and that's why we're still  trying to raise money around it and  that's sort of what everyone was  predicting to that we wouldn't get all  of our ads back and it probably wouldn't  stay the same as it was at the very  beginning when we were losing 99% of our  ads yes it would be somewhere in the  middle there and I think the problem  with that is it's a small victory so it  may cause some channels to get content  with the amount of ground that they were  able to make up yes indeed and we are  it's not a matter of being content it's  that we need to keep making up the money  so again there's a  few things you can do to help the David  Pakman show  recover the money that we've lost number  one of course there's membership you go  to david pakman.com slash membership if  the normal rates are high for you use  the coupon code  I voted seventeen number two you go to  patreon patreon is simpler than  membership you just pledge any amount of  money you want per month a dollar two  dollars ten dollars whatever you want  patreon.com slash david pakman show  number three if you ever shop on  amazon.com  go to david pakman.com slash amazon  before you shop sends us a kickback for  everything you buy number four if you  have a YouTube red subscription watch  our videos we get a fraction of your  subscription every time you watch one of  our one of our videos and lastly you can  get david pakman show gear including  coffee t-shirts bumper stickers zip up  hoodies etc at david pakman.com slash  gear let's very quickly just check in on  how patreon is doing we had crested the  1500 patron mark at the end of april but  as often happens when a new month kicks  in and patrons are charged a lot of  people's credit cards have expired or  get declined or whatever so that has  brought us back down below the 1500  patron mark so please help us keep that  growing at patreon.com slash david  pakman show even if you can only pledge  a dollar do it and you know I'm going to  try to make these updates less more  seldom because I don't want to fatigue  the audience but we do need to talk  about what's going on with the show and  remind me what the mark is before we  have to come into the show with crazy  hairstyles so if and when we get to  2,000 patrons I will do an entire show  with my puffed up hair which I put up on  my Instagram when we get to 2,000  patrons I'm willing to do that
 

